# Cursor Rules for Jay Ess Traders Project

## Project Context
This is a Next.js 14 digital visiting card for Jay Ess Traders, a tiles/bathware retailer.

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all new files
- Use functional components with hooks
- Prefer arrow functions
- Use Tailwind for styling (no inline styles)
- Follow shadcn/ui patterns for components

## File Organization
- Components go in `app/components/`
- UI primitives go in `components/ui/`
- Utilities go in `app/lib/`
- Configuration in `app/data/site.ts`

## Best Practices
- Always use Next.js Image for images
- Lazy load heavy components
- Keep components under 200 lines
- Extract reusable logic to hooks
- Use Framer Motion for animations (keep subtle)

## Configuration
- Edit `app/data/site.ts` for content changes
- Never hardcode contact info in components
- Always use siteConfig for data

## Performance
- Optimize images before committing
- Keep bundle size minimal
- Use dynamic imports for modals/drawers
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders

## Testing
- Test on mobile first
- Verify all CTAs work
- Check Lighthouse scores
- Test on slow 3G

## Dependencies
- Use pnpm for package management
- Avoid adding unnecessary packages
- Check bundle impact before adding deps

